questions.question_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (150:2.5);
\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=150,radius=2.5];
\pic[draw,"$150^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=2] {angle=A--O--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the area of this sector, correct to $2$ decimal places.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (72:2.5);
\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ m}$};
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=72,radius=2.5];
\pic[draw,"$72^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=2.4] {angle=A--O--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the area of this sector in exact form, in terms of $\pi$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw (O) -- (2.5,0) node[midway,below] {$6\text{ mm}$};
\draw (O) -- (0,2.5);
\draw (2.5,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=2.5];
\draw (0.32,0) -- (0.32,0.32) -- (0,0.32);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the area of this quadrant in exact form, in terms of $\pi$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\draw (-2.5,0) -- (2.5,0) node[midway,below] {$20\text{ cm}$};
\draw (2.5,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=2.5];
\fill (0,0) circle (1.6pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the area of this semicircle, correct to $2$ decimal places.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (130:2.5);
\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (130:2.5) arc[start angle=130,end angle=360,radius=2.5];
\pic[draw,"$130^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.65cm,angle eccentricity=2.1] {angle=A--O--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The angle marked is the **exterior** angle of the sector. Find the area of the sector, correct to $1$ decimal place.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (45:2.5);
\draw[dashed,gray] (O) circle (2.5);
\draw (O) -- (A);
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=45,radius=2.5];
\pic[draw,"$45^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=2.9] {angle=A--O--B};
\fill (O) circle (1.6pt);
\draw[dashed] (-2.5,0) -- (-2.5,-3.00);
\draw[dashed] (2.5,0) -- (2.5,-3.00);
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.5,-3.00) -- (2.5,-3.00) node[midway,below] {$24\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The dashed circle is the circle the sector was cut from, and its diameter is marked. Find the area of the sector in exact form, in terms of $\pi$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw[gray] (0,0) circle (2.3);
\foreach \a in {0,30,60,90,120,150,180,210,240,270,300,330} {\draw[gray] (O) -- (\a:2.3);}
\draw[thick] (O) -- (0:2.3) node[midway,below] {$14\text{ cm}$};
\draw[thick] (O) -- (30:2.3);
\draw[thick] (0:2.3) arc[start angle=0,end angle=30,radius=2.3];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A circular cake is cut into $12$ equal slices. Find the exact area of one slice, in terms of $\pi$.
